---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { release, discoverySources, url } from '../lib/publication';
const builtAt = new Date().toISOString();
const systems = [
 ['Rainfall', release.observations.filter(o => o.metricId.startsWith('rainfall')).length],
 ['Reservoir storage', release.observations.filter(o => o.metricId.startsWith('reservoir')).length],
 ['Groundwater', release.observations.filter(o => o.metricId.startsWith('groundwater')).length],
 ['River flow', release.observations.filter(o => o.metricId.startsWith('river')).length],
 ['Household service', release.observations.filter(o => o.metricId.startsWith('service')).length],
 ['Water quality', release.observations.filter(o => o.metricId.startsWith('quality')).length],
 ['Forecasts', release.observations.filter(o => o.status === 'forecast').length],
] as const;
---
<Site title="Coverage and freshness"><PageHeader title="Coverage & freshness" eyebrow="Data status" description="The publication's observation, retrieval, review and build dates are separate clocks. Missing evidence does not imply normal conditions." /><section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="grid-3"><div class="empty-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Approved snapshot</p><h3>{release.releaseId}</h3><p>{release.observations.length} observations tied to reviewed public claims.</p></div><div class="empty-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Agent claim check</p><h3>{release.reviewedAt ? release.reviewedAt.slice(0,10) : 'Not recorded'}</h3><p>Agent check date is not an observation or provider publication date. Human editorial sign-off has not been recorded.</p></div><div class="empty-panel"><p class="eyebrow">Static build</p><h3>{builtAt.slice(0,10)}</h3><p>Build timestamp <time datetime={builtAt}>{builtAt}</time>. It does not refresh source observations.</p></div></div><h2 style="margin-top:3rem">Observation and source clocks</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Place / indicator</th><th>Observed period</th><th>Provider publication</th><th>Retrieved</th><th>Agent claim check</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody>{release.observations.map(o => {const s=release.sources.find(source => source.id === o.sourceId);const c=release.claims.find(claim => claim.id === o.claimId);const g=release.geographies.find(geo => geo.id === o.geographyId);return <tr><td>{g?.name || o.geographyId}<br /><small>{o.metricId.replaceAll('_',' ')}</small></td><td>{o.periodStart.slice(0,10)} to {o.periodEnd.slice(0,10)}</td><td>{s?.publicationDate?.slice(0,10) || 'Unknown'}</td><td>{s?.retrievedAt?.slice(0,10) || 'Unknown'}</td><td>{c?.reviewedAt?.slice(0,10) || 'Unknown'}</td><td><a href={url(`/sources/${o.sourceId}/`)}>Record ↗</a></td></tr>})}</tbody></table></div>{release.observations.length === 0 && <div class="empty-panel"><p>No approved observation rows are present in this build.</p></div>}<h2 style="margin-top:3rem">Coverage by system</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Current public status</th><th>Next evidence needed</th></tr></thead><tbody>{systems.map(([name,count]) => <tr><td>{name}</td><td>{count ? `${count} approved observation${count === 1 ? '' : 's'}` : 'No current approved observation'}</td><td>{count ? 'See each source record and definition' : 'Exact dated source, matching geography, definitions and review'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="small muted">A published rainfall departure is a weather signal, not direct evidence for storage, groundwater, service, health or an official drought declaration.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="shell"><p class="eyebrow">Discovery coverage</p><h2>Access is not approval</h2><p>{discoverySources.length} source leads are recorded. Their retrieval status, document rights and exact observation periods need separate checking.</p><a href={url('/sources/')}>Inspect each source lead ↗</a></div></section></Site>
